# oosh E2E Specification: Tier 4 Real-World Scenarios
# Author: test_writer_e2e_1
# Standard: openOODA House Laws (Page Rule: 16-256 lines)

[T4-SCN: Real-World Scenarios]
- T4-SCN-01: Developer Failure & Autonomous Recovery
  Step 1: Execute failing command (e.g. invalid git branch).
  Step 2: Failure envelope records non-zero status and stderr.
  Step 3: User calls remedy.
  Step 4: Remedy displays double-lined card with Algiz rune and diagnosis.
  Step 5: Remedy proposes fix; user accepts and executes.
  Step 6: Command succeeds; telemetry badge shows duration and success glyph.

- T4-SCN-02: Ambient Natural Language Cockpit Session
  Step 1: Launch oosh; ambient status dock renders git branch and posture.
  Step 2: Enter intent query (? list rust files).
  Step 3: Intent scanner intercepts prefix; context engine scans directory.
  Step 4: Synthesizer translates query into POSIX command.
  Step 5: Safety rating displays SAFE green badge with preview card.
  Step 6: User presses Y; command executes; telemetry badge output.

- T4-SCN-03: Headless Varlink Autonomous Agent Orchestration
  Step 1: Daemon binds /run/oosh/control.sock.
  Step 2: External agent connects and queries GetInfo introspection.
  Step 3: Agent calls QueryPosture to audit shell posture.
  Step 4: Agent dispatches ExecuteCommand with parameters.
  Step 5: Command output and exit code returned over NUL-delimited stream.
  Step 6: Daemon remains alive and cleans up socket upon shutdown.

- T4-SCN-04: Flight Recorder Postmortem Crash Autopsy
  Step 1: Execute sequence of 5 maintenance and build commands.
  Step 2: Intermediate command fails with non-zero exit code.
  Step 3: User invokes autopsy (or bb).
  Step 4: Double-lined card renders with Hagalaz rune.
  Step 5: Chronological log displays all 5 executions with exact timings.

- T4-SCN-05: Ambient Terminal Session with Capability Audit & Builtin Navigation
  Step 1: User runs caps builtin to inspect unforgeable capability tokens.
  Step 2: Double-lined card renders with Tiwaz rune.
  Step 3: User runs whereami to verify host node and location.
  Step 4: User navigates directories using bare .. and take.
  Step 5: Ambient prompt updates path and git status dynamically.
  Step 6: User enters :q to terminate session cleanly.
